/Title (My whole life changed when I woke up to the reality of the factory farm and slaughterhouse industry. My initial research explored solutions to end plastic production at its root while promoting alternative organic-based products \(like mycelium and seaweed packaging\). However, as I looked into plastic's destructive nature, I started noticing other harmful industries. I started mapping similarities between the energetic signature  of *how* plastic was made \(violent extraction through fracking and the invasion of nature\) and the energetic signature of factory farms, the treatment of the homeless, how poverty is subtly passed on and structurally instituted, the obsession with violence and domination through the military-industrial complex, and lastly, the normalization of modern-day slavery through covert and overt intercontinental operations.)
